##Overall Workflow
A multi-agent thaqt is given a client brief, real product images, a moodboard, and the brand's asset library.
The tool runs four AI agents in sequence to produce a full set of image and video prompts. One complete set per product, organised into folders to generate.

---
##The Agents
Agent 1. Brand Analysis: Reads the inputs provided (client brief, moodboard, product images, asset library) 
It then analayses the brand's established visual identity such as lighting, composition, colour grading and casting. Then decides the exact visual style guide for shots, images and video to pass onto the next agents.

Agent 2. Product Analysis: It analyses each product given and extracts every visible detial such as, shape, colour, material, hardware etc. 
It then builds per product spec to pass onto the next agent. 

Agent 3. Prompt Writing: It uses the visual guide (agent 1) and per product spec (agent 2) to write scene-focused prompts.
Will deliberately avoid redescribing the product in vivid detail. (causes AI distorition)
Instead it will instruct the image generator that will be used to refernce the given product image. 
This allows the prompt budget to be spent on the scene, lighting and atmosphere instead on the product alone. 

Agent 4. Output: Saves all the prompts into .txt files for each product. Making it ready to paste into Higgsfield. 

---
##Inputs
The tool provids questions on the client, which I have to answer for the brief. 
Then I provide files for the product images, the brands "moodboard" and the brand's asset library containing real photography for the tool to refernce. 

---
##Ouputs
As mentioned, agent 4 outputs per product files. Each containing catalogue shot prompts, website image prompts and a banner video prompt for the wesbite. 

---
##Why each agent is given seperate responsibilites 
If they weren't given their own individual responsibilites the tool would conclude with shallower decisions which would create very weak outputs. 
By having an agent per role, it allows each agent to focus solely on its one given task with no distractions. So agent 1 gets to just focus on analysing the brand, agent 2 gets to only analyase the product and etc. This deliberate decison allows them to pass on a clean output to the next agent. 
This allows each agent to work together to create throughly thought through creative direction for the client, instead of a messy output due to one overwhelmed agent doing 4 different jobs. 
